=== P3 Modal / dialog 0003 ChangelogModal (Android) ===

Surface : ChangelogModal  (registry id "changelog-modal", category "modals-dialogs", slug "ChangelogModal")
Web spec: web/src/components/feedback/ChangelogModal.tsx
Data    : web/src/hooks/useChangelog.ts + web/src/generated/changelog.ts (static catalog + local ack store)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CAPABILITY (BLOCKED clause check)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Required: Jetpack Compose + Material 3 + Kotlin 2.2.x.  AVAILABLE on this runner:
  - JDK 21 (Android Studio JBR), Android SDK at %LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk (adb + sdkmanager on PATH)
  - Kotlin 2.4.0 (>= 2.2.x), AGP 8.9.2, Compose BOM 2026.04.01, Material 3 (gradle/libs.versions.toml)
  - minSdk 26 (Android 8, API 26+ per prompt), targetSdk/compileSdk 36
Baseline `:android:assembleRelease` is GREEN (pre-change).  => NOT blocked.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PATH / MODULE RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's templated paths do not match this repo; corrected to the repo's real,
gate-compliant locations (evidence cited), NOT worked around:

  1. Gradle module: prompt gate says `:app:` -> real module is `:android`.
     Evidence: apps/android/settings.gradle.kts L33-36
       include(":android"); project(":android").projectDir = file("app")
       ("every P3/A* prompt gate addresses `:android:`").
     `:app:assembleRelease` fails with "project 'app' not found"; `:android:` is used below.
     (Matches the sibling p3-android-dashboard-widgets-* logs.)

  2. Source location: the surface bundle lives at the prompt's mandated allowed-files
     directory  apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/modals-dialogs/ChangelogModal/
     but declares the idiomatic package  io.teslasync.android.modalsdialogs.changelogmodal
     (a hyphen + PascalCase segment cannot form a valid Kotlin package). detekt's
     InvalidPackageDeclaration + ktlint's filename rule are suppressed at file scope on the
     affected files, exactly as the sibling feature-view surfaces (e.g. AccordionSection) do.
     Co-located tests use the matching, path-valid package directory under src/test + src/androidTest.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STATES (every reachable state rendered — no fabricated network lifecycle)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
useChangelog is a static-catalog + local-acknowledgement store (build-time-generated
@/generated/changelog + a localStorage seen-version/last-shown record), NOT a remote query.
There is therefore no loading / error / stale / offline network lifecycle to render —
modelling one would be fabricated state the web source never has (covenant #9 "no silent
drift"), exactly as the sibling AccordionSection surface documents. The genuinely reachable
render states are reproduced and tested:
  [state]  first-visit      -> "Welcome!..." subtitle + full history (ChangelogRender.FirstVisit)
  [state]  since-last-visit -> "{{count}} new release(s)..." subtitle + the unseen delta (SinceLastVisit)
  [state]  empty            -> catalog with no releases -> friendly EmptyState, never a blank box (Empty)
  [branch] per-entry collapsed / expanded (web `defaultOpen={idx < 2}`, chevron rotate-180)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILES (the ChangelogModal surface bundle + its tests)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
main/.../com/teslasync/modals-dialogs/ChangelogModal/
  ChangelogModalModel.kt    pure model: ChangelogChange/Release/Section/Badge/ChangeType types,
                            ChangelogAck, ChangelogRender, ChangelogStrings + ChangelogEntryAffordances,
                            ChangelogSource seam + DefaultChangelogSource + ChangelogAckStore (P1/S8),
                            ChangelogModalModel (compareVersions w/ pre-release, newReleases, visibleReleases,
                            isFirstVisit, canAutoShow, shouldAutoShow, groupChanges, defaultExpanded,
                            markSeen/stampShown, classify), resolveOptional. No Compose/Android/HTTP.
  ChangelogModalCatalog.kt  embedded release catalog (native analogue of @/generated/changelog):
                            all 6 releases / 189 changes, AUTOGENERATED + verbatim from CHANGELOG.md.
  ChangelogModal.kt         Compose view: ChangelogModalController (imperative open), stateful ChangelogModal
                            (auto-show + controller paths, ack semantics, view.opened telemetry P1/S11),
                            stateless ChangelogModalContent + ChangelogEntryCard/Body, SharedPreferences
                            ack store, i18n resolvers, 3 @Preview (first-visit / since-last-visit / empty).
test/.../modalsdialogs/changelogmodal/
  ChangelogModalModelTest.kt      34 tests (semver/pre-release, derivations, gating, grouping, reducers,
                                  classify, strings/affordance selectors, resolveOptional, default source,
                                  embedded-catalog integrity).
androidTest/.../modalsdialogs/changelogmodal/
  ChangelogModalUiTest.kt         6 UI/a11y tests (first-visit/empty render, expand/collapse, Got-it
                                  callback, header-is-button + state description). Runs under
                                  connectedAndroidTest; the gate runs testReleaseUnitTest only.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY EVIDENCE (web -> native, file:symbol)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[data]   useChangelog            -> ChangelogSource seam bound by DefaultChangelogSource to ChangelogCatalog
                                    + SharedPrefsChangelogAckStore (ChangelogModal.kt / ChangelogModalModel.kt)
[data]   @/generated/changelog   -> ChangelogCatalog.releases / LATEST_VERSION (ChangelogModalCatalog.kt)
[logic]  compareVersions         -> ChangelogModalModel.compareVersions (semver + pre-release-before-release)
[logic]  newEntries/hasUnseen    -> ChangelogModalModel.newReleases / hasUnseen
[logic]  visibleEntries          -> ChangelogModalModel.visibleReleases
[logic]  isFirstVisit            -> ChangelogModalModel.isFirstVisit
[logic]  canAutoShow + 24h       -> ChangelogModalModel.canAutoShow (AUTO_SHOW_THROTTLE_MS)
[logic]  auto-show effect guard  -> ChangelogModalModel.shouldAutoShow (+ suppressAutoShow = [data-tour-active])
[logic]  SECTION_ORDER grouping  -> ChangelogModalModel.groupChanges (drops empty sections)
[logic]  defaultOpen={idx<2}     -> ChangelogModalModel.defaultExpanded
[logic]  markSeen / stampShown   -> ChangelogModalModel.markSeen / stampShown
[event]  OPEN_CHANGELOG_MODAL    -> ChangelogModalController.open() (+ rememberChangelogModalController)
[link]   github .../releases     -> ChangelogModalModel.RELEASES_URL via LocalUriHandler.openUri
[i18n]   changelog.modal.title   -> R.string.translation_changelog_modal_title ("What's new in TeslaSync")
[i18n]   subtitleFirstVisit      -> R.string.translation_changelog_modal_subtitleFirstVisit
[i18n]   subtitleSinceLastVisit  -> R.string.translation_changelog_modal_subtitleSinceLastVisit (%1$s count)
[i18n]   viewFull / gotIt        -> R.string.translation_changelog_modal_viewFull / _gotIt
[i18n]   badges.{latest..beta}   -> R.string.translation_changelog_badges_{latest,stable,beta}
[i18n]   sections.{added..sec}   -> R.string.translation_changelog_sections_{added,changed,fixed,removed,deprecated,security}
[i18n]   close affordance        -> R.string.translation_a11y_closeDialog
[badge]  BADGE_VARIANT map       -> badgeVariant (latest->Success, stable->Info, beta->Warning)
[dot]    SECTION_DOT colors      -> sectionDotColor (theme status tokens + tertiary for deprecated)
[a11y]   role=button/aria-expanded -> merged header Role.Button + stateDescription + onClickLabel
[telem]  view.opened slug=ChangelogModal -> logger.info on open (P1/S11, redacting logger)

Note: the placeholder scan flags one legitimate verbatim CHANGELOG.md token ("changeme placeholders",
0.3.0 Security) — opted out with `// parity:allow` (PLACEHOLDER_ALLOWED=1), real release content, not a stub.

